# Caddy in front of the Pharos API (SEC-07, ADR-0046, docs/despliegue.md).
#
# Caddy ends TLS and passes X-Forwarded-Proto and X-Forwarded-For to the API,
# which runs with TRUST_PROXY=true and refuses plain http in production.
# - A public domain (PHAROS_DOMAIN=pharos.example.com, ports 80 and 443 open):
#   Caddy gets and renews a Let's Encrypt certificate by itself.
# - localhost or an IP: Caddy uses its own CA ("tls internal") by itself.
# - An internal name (pharos.company.lan): uncomment `tls internal`. The app
#   connects once Windows trusts Caddy's root certificate
#   (docs/despliegue.md, «Certificado interno»).
# Plain http on port 80 is redirected to https.

{$PHAROS_DOMAIN:localhost} {
	# tls internal
	encode zstd gzip
	reverse_proxy {$PHAROS_API:api:3000}
}
